    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The phases include Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the tender requirements for a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout, our project management approach aligns well. our company's past references in the public sector and healthcare, such as the regional council and regional hospital group projects, demonstrate our company's capability to manage similar engagements. our company's consortium partners, including OuraneCloud for hosting and Ligeo Santé for health-IT integration, enhance our company's delivery capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering the global budget of 900,000 over 5 years and the need for controlled annual operating costs, our company's must ensure efficient project execution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering our company's available capacity, with a dedicated team including a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, our company's can manage the project scope. our projected project timeline would likely follow our company's standard phase-gate structure: 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Framing: Framing involves understanding the client's needs and defining the project scope." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's experience, Framing could be completed within 2-3 months. 2." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Design: During Framing, our company's would design the AI assistance solution tailored to the hospital's specific requirements. design might take around 4-6 months, considering the complexity of integrating with existing systems like SIH/DPI and ensuring compliance with health data regulations. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Pilot: The pilot phase, as required by The tender, would involve deploying the AI assistance solution in a limited perimeter (one or two departments) to test the AI assistance solution efficacy and identify areas for improvement." ;
